@@ -33,6 +33,23 @@ edge vocabulary: `displaced-from`, `resolves-under`, `dropped-under`,
 **Atomicity:** one idea per node. If `split_suggested` comes back true, split
 the node into linked nodes — never trim or compress.
 
+## Settle
+When a position, challenge, or question has been decided — "we went with Redis",
+"that objection is moot", "this branch is dropped" — call `mindmap_resolve` with
+the node_id, disposition (`resolved` | `dropped`), and a short `resolution_summary`.
+This writes the durable branch status (the source of truth for open loops and
+resume), and, if you pass `resolved_by_memory_id` (another member of the map that
+settled it), draws a `resolves-under` / `dropped-under` edge from the resolver
+onto the settled node. A bare `mindmap_link` with a `resolves-under` kind does
+NOT settle a branch — only `mindmap_resolve` does. Settling the map root itself
+is not allowed here; graduating the whole map is `mindmap_close`.
+
+## Resume cheaply
+`mindmap_get(map_key=..., since=<last cursor>)` returns only the nodes touched
+since that event id, the current `cursor` (always), the `resolved` set of
+branches settled in that window, and open loops over the whole map. Store the
+returned `cursor` and reuse it on the next resume.
+
 ## Ratify
 When the user endorses a position, record it on the node:
 `ratification_strength` ∈ `survived-challenge` > `explicit-endorse` >
